   171	def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
   172	    """
   173	    Rebuild a staircase of enlarged blocks from a 1D edge legend.
   174	
   175	    Input structure:
   176	    - bg is the dominant background color.
   177	    - Near the top-left border, the legend is a single row or a single column of isolated pixels on a step-2 lattice.
   178	    - Elsewhere, only two uniformly colored square blocks of the larger pattern are already present.
   179	
   180	    Rule:
   181	    - Read the edge legend as an ordered 1D color sequence.
   182	    - Expand that sequence into a 2D staircase: a top-edge row colors staircase columns, while a left-edge column colors staircase rows.
   183	    - Use the existing blocks to infer the enlarged lattice step and base offset, then add every missing block from the expanded staircase.
